# Copy to .env.local for local development (never commit real values). On Vercel set the same names in Project Settings > Environment Variables.
# "secret" = never expose to the browser, never commit, rotate if leaked. tests/unit/env-example.test.ts fails if code uses a variable that is not listed here.

# ---- Supabase ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project URL, e.g. https://abcd1234.supabase.co (local: http://127.0.0.1:54321). Public. Used by the browser and server clients, the middleware
# and the Content-Security-Policy. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are baked in at BUILD time: set it BEFORE the first Vercel build and redeploy after changing it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# The project's anon (public) key. Public by design; row-level security is what protects the data.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SECRET. The service-role key bypasses row-level security. Used only on the server: audit writes, the PayFast notification, the cron worker.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---- The app's own address -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin with no trailing slash (https://practice.example.co.za). Required in production: used in emailed links, the PayFast return/notify URLs.
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---- PayFast (card payments) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Merchant id and key from the PayFast dashboard (Settings > Integration). The key is SECRET.
PAYFAST_MERCHANT_ID=
PAYFAST_MERCHANT_KEY=
# SECRET. Must equal the passphrase set in the PayFast dashboard. REQUIRED outside the sandbox.
PAYFAST_PASSPHRASE=
# "true" talks to sandbox.payfast.co.za. Anything else (including unset) is LIVE.
PAYFAST_SANDBOX=true

# ---- Scheduled worker (reminders, overdue tasks, outgoing email) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET. Long random value (openssl rand -hex 32). Vercel sends it as "Authorization: Bearer ..." on cron calls; an external scheduler must too.
CRON_SECRET=

# ---- Email and SMS -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both needed to send real email (Resend adapter, a placeholder choice). In production, without both nothing is sent and email rows stay pending. EMAIL_API_KEY is SECRET.
EMAIL_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=
# "true" only once a real SMS provider is wired in (Phase 1 has none).
SMS_ACTIVE=

# ---- End-to-end tests (Playwright; tests/e2e, README "Running the end-to-end tests") ------------------------------------------------------------
# Not used by the app. Without the three E2E_SUPABASE_* values the e2e specs skip themselves. Use a throwaway staging project or a local `supabase start`, NEVER production.
# The app under test (default http://localhost:3000).
# E2E_BASE_URL=
# 1 = start `npm run dev` for the run.
# E2E_START_SERVER=
# The Supabase project the app under test talks to. E2E_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY is SECRET.
# E2E_SUPABASE_URL=
# E2E_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# E2E_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# Password of the seeded demo accounts (default: the one printed in supabase/seed.sql).
# E2E_PASSWORD=
# Optional: PayFast passphrase / merchant id of the app under test, to check that a signed notification from a non-PayFast address is refused.
# E2E_PAYFAST_PASSPHRASE=
# E2E_PAYFAST_MERCHANT_ID=
# 1 = create the workflow A patient through the admin API instead of the /register page (hosted projects limit confirmation emails per hour).
# E2E_ADMIN_CREATE_PATIENT=
# Set to enable the registration test in booking.spec.ts (creates a real auth user).
# E2E_CAN_REGISTER=
# 1 = hide the "E2E environment not set" notice.
# E2E_QUIET=
# 1 = FAIL the run (non-zero exit) when the E2E variables above are missing, instead of skipping everything. Use it in CI and staging gates.
# E2E_REQUIRE=
